# FP-reasoning: HIGH, plain. CVE-2017-6334 Netgear DGN1000/DGN2200 unauth RCE
# via setup.cgi (the `?next_file=` parameter loads a config file but the
# attendant `?todo=` + cmd= injects shell). Mass-Mirai-scanned (34 real-
# traffic hits in AUDIT-REALGAP). Clean-room from advisory. Scope http.uri.
# raw. fast_pattern "/setup.cgi" + pcre requires the `next_file=` exploit
# parameter + a shell-metachar in cmd. Negative: a benign /setup.cgi GET
# without next_file → reaches pcre, rejected → silent.
alert http any any -> any any (msg:"KNOWN-CVE Netgear DGN1000/DGN2200 setup.cgi unauth RCE (CVE-2017-6334) [high]"; flow:established,to_server; http.uri.raw; content:"/setup.cgi"; nocase; fast_pattern; pcre:"/\/setup\.cgi\?[^\r\n]{0,200}?next_file=[^&\r\n]{0,80}?\.htm[^\r\n]{0,200}?(?:cmd=|curpath=)[^\r\n]{0,80}?[\x60\x24\x7c\x3b]/i"; classtype:attempted-admin; metadata: asset_category infra, owasp A06-Vulnerable-and-Outdated-Components, attack_target Server, mitre_tactic_id TA0001, mitre_tactic_name Initial-Access, mitre_technique_id T1190, mitre_technique_name Exploit-Public-Facing-Application, kill_chain Exploitation, confidence high, signature_severity Critical, deployment Perimeter, network_mode plain, cve CVE-2017-6334, poc_ref tests/poc/9300051_netgear-dgn-rce/poc.sh, tag netgear, created_at 2026_05_22, updated_at 2026_05_22, author huntingyuk; sid:9300051; rev:1;)
